Cutwright deliberately does NOT ship an FFmpeg binary. Common prebuilt FFmpeg
distributions (ffmpeg-static, gyan.dev, evermeet, most Homebrew bottles) are
compiled with --enable-gpl (x264/x265); redistributing one inside this
Apache-2.0 application would place the combined distribution under the GPL.
Cutwright therefore invokes whatever FFmpeg the user has installed, as a separate
process, and tells them how to install it if it is missing. If a future release
wants a bundled binary, it must be a custom LGPL build (no --enable-gpl, no
x264/x265) relying on hardware encoders — see docs/decisions/0002-ffmpeg-licensing.md.

